Keep this repo's runtime-only env knobs out of the torch.compile cache key.

compile_factors() hashes every registered VLLM_* variable not in
ignored_factors, so a knob this repo registers only to read it through
envs -- the engine-stall watchdog's timeout, the Mamba checkpoint-retention
toggle in the KV block manager, the DFlash2 chain log interval, an unused
directory path -- invalidated the whole compile cache whenever its value
changed: a cold compile (~227 s against ~150 s) for a setting no compiled
graph reads (syv-ai/HyperQwen #183). The deprecated env spelling of
--prefix-cache-retention-interval joins them, matching
CacheConfig.compute_hash, which already leaves that field out.

Cut by hand against 0.29.0 with the series applied (not an export from the fork).

diff --git a/envs.py b/envs.py
index 2dc6a5c..c465e34 100755
--- a/envs.py
+++ b/envs.py
@@ -2359,6 +2359,16 @@ def compile_factors() -> dict[str, object]:
         "VLLM_CACHE_ROOT",
         # Runtime memory-plan persistence; does not affect compiled graphs.
         "VLLM_ENABLE_STARTUP_PLAN",
+        # This repo's runtime-only knobs (syv-ai/HyperQwen #183): read by the engine
+        # loop, the KV block manager, a log timer or not at all, never by traced code.
+        # Hashed, each new value cost a cold torch.compile (~227 s against ~150 s).
+        "VLLM_ENGINE_STALL_SENTINEL_S",
+        "VLLM_MAMBA_ALIGN_KEEP_CHECKPOINTS",
+        "VLLM_DFLASH2_CHAIN_LOG_SEC",
+        "VLLM_MARLIN_TUNE_DIR",
+        # The deprecated env spelling of --prefix-cache-retention-interval, which
+        # CacheConfig.compute_hash already leaves out of the hash for the same reason.
+        "VLLM_PREFIX_CACHE_RETENTION_INTERVAL",
         # Location-only derived paths: where a cache/config directory lives
         # cannot affect compiled artifacts, and hashing them means relocating
         # HOME or the XDG roots silently invalidates every compile cache
